The amplification/readout layer can provide an amplification of \(1000\) to \(3000\) when the electrons avalanche in the high field. The wire direction is chosen to best determine the momentum of very high transverse momentum particles whose tracks do not curve much in the magnetic field. Fig. 2.6 shows the anode pad plane with one full sector. The pad dimensions are also optimized to the best position resolution perpendicular to radial tracks. The width of the pad is chosen such that the induced charge from an avalanche point on the anode wires shares most of its signal with three pads. The outer radius pad sub-sectors was designed with continuous pad coverage to achieve the best possible energy loss (\(dE/dx\)) resolution. This is optimal because the full track ionization signal is collected and more ionization electrons improve statistics on the \(dE/dx\) measurement. It also improves tracking resolution due to anti-correlation of errors between pad rows. The outer radius sub-sectors are arranged on a rectangular grid with a pitch of 6.7 mm along the wires and 20.0 mm perpendicular to the wires and

