### \(P_{x}\) calculation

Jet correlations are studied with respect to high-\(p_{T}\) trigger particles, serving as proxies for jets [9, 92]. High-\(p_{T}\) particle production is strongly biased toward surface of the collision zone [92]. The away-side jet partner, therefore, traverses the entire volume suffering maximal interactions with the medium. Because of the broad distribution of the underlining parton kinematics, the away-side jet direction is "random" in \(\eta\) relative to the trigger particle. It is therefore difficult to distinguish jet signal from the underlying background-the large, azimuthally anisotropic background has to be manually subtracted, with large uncertainties, using measured anisotropy parameters. The away-side jet direction can be localized by requiring a second high-\(p_{T}\) particle back-to-back the first one. However, by doing so, the back-to-back dijets are likely tangential to the collision zone [35, 93], demolishing the purpose of studying jet-medium interactions.

In this analysis, we impose a less biasing requirement of a large recoil transverse momentum (\(P_{x}\)) from the high-\(p_{T}\) trigger particle, within a given \(\eta\) range, to enhance the away-side jet population in acceptance. \(P_{x}\) is given by

\[P_{x}|_{\eta_{1}}^{\eta_{2}}=\sum_{\eta_{1}<\eta<\eta_{2},|\phi-\phi_{\text{ trig}}|>\pi/2}p_{T}\,\text{cos}(\phi-\phi_{\text{trig}})\cdot\frac{1}{\epsilon}\, \tag{3.1}\]

Where all particles (\(0.15<p_{T}<10\) GeV/c measured in the TPC) are included. Only particles on the away-side of the trigger particle are included in the \(P_{x}\) calculation so that the trigger particle is disentangled from the away-side jet and the \(\eta\) distribution of the trigger particle is unbiased by \(P_{x}\) selection. The single-particle relative acceptance\(\times\)detection efficiency \(\epsilon\) (Eq. 3.2) is applied. It depends on \(z_{vtx}\), collision centrality, \(p_{T}\), \(\eta\) and \(\phi\), and has time dependent variations [94]. Because our \(P_{x}\) cut is only relative, the absolute efficiency correction is not applied.

