#### 3.5.1 \(\phi\)-dependent efficiency correction

The TPC is made of 12 separated sectors on each side of the endcaps. Some of the \(\phi\) bins are low in efficiency because they are within sector boundaries. Deficit sectors due to electronics failure would also reduce tracking efficiency. If we do not do \(\phi\)-dependent efficiency correction, then the large \(P_{x}\) cut would be mainly cutting on detector deficit.

Single-particle \(\phi\) distributions are histogramed as a function of run, centrality and particle transverse momentum and for east-side TPC (\(\eta<0\)) and west-side TPC (\(\eta>0\)) separately. Fig. 3.7 shows single-particle \(\phi\) distributions with \(1<p_{T}<1.5\ GeV/c\) and \(runid=12171001\) in \(0-5\)% central Au+Au collisions. East-side TPC and west-side TPC have different efficiency, so the corrections have been done separately.

