Figure 4.8: Possible azimuthal distribution of hadrons with respect to the jet axis.

Figure 4.7: Width of the diagonal and off-diagonal projections of the three-particle correlations with \(3<p_{T}^{trig}<10\) GeV\(/c\) and \(2<p_{T}^{asso}<3\) GeV\(/c\).

flected by the medium flow. Another explanation would be nuclear \(k_{T}\) effect. Incident nucleons suffer from multiple scattering before the initial parton hard scattering. The parton-parton system has a net transverse momentum and therefore dijets are not back-to-back when produced. Initial- and final-state effects in Au+Au collisions can be separated through studies of \(d\)+Au collisions.
* Intra-jet correlations: The width of the off-diagonal is similar between near- and away-side and no centrality dependence is found. It seems that there is little jet modifications. The broadening of the away-side jet correlations is mainly caused by nuclear \(k_{T}\) effect and/or jets deflected by medium flow.

